I walk down to the beach.
Many people have already arrived for the evening's party.
I look for Eva and Peter in the crowd.
Suddenly I see them down by the water, and I hurry over there.
"Have you had a good birthday week?" Peter asks with a smile.
"Yes, it has been absolutely fantastic," I answer happily.
Eva opens a small basket.
"I bought fresh strawberries at the market this morning," she says.
"Have you ever tasted Danish summer strawberries?"
"No, I have never tried that," I say and take a berry.
It tastes incredibly sweet and reminds me of summer.
Right at that moment, a man lights the big bonfire.
The flames grow quickly and stretch high up toward the sky.
It was cold earlier, but now the fire has warmed up the air.
The glowing heat quickly chases away the cold from the coast.
We stand close together and look into the flames for a long time.
I think about how I have now lived here in the city for six months.
My first month here was dark, but this bright summer evening is perfect.
